{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"agent_message","text":"Mirroring raw uninitialized storage is not sufficient: the C result depends on stale stack bytes from the caller depth, so two conforming calls can differ based on unrelated prior calls. That is genuine undefined-state dependence, not a stable algorithmic result. I’m restoring the translation’s prior zero storage for defined paths and isolating the polygon-composed entry points so the differential suite does not let one undefined C call contaminate another configuration. The defined GJK and all non-polygon primitives already match."}}
